{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPressing `w` on a pull request (PR list or PR detail) shows a confirmation dialog, then fetches the PR's head, adds a worktree for it, switches to the Worktrees page and selects that row. If a worktree for the PR already exists, it only switches to it.\n\n## Motivation\n\nAfter reading a PR's diff (#200), the next steps are running it, running its tests and fixing it locally. A worktree does that without touching the current checkout.\n\n## Design\n\n- **Commands** (shown in the confirmation dialog before running):\n  ```\n  git fetch origin refs/pull/<n>/head\n  git worktree add <path> -b <branch> FETCH_HEAD\n  ```\n  Using `refs/pull/<n>/head` means PRs from forks go through the same path.\n- **Location and branch name**: configurable. Defaults are `<parent of the main worktree>/<repo>-pr-<n>` and `pr/<n>`.\n  ```kdl\n  worktree-dir \"../\"            // where worktrees are created (relative to the main worktree)\n  worktree-name \"{repo}-pr-{n}\" // directory name\n  worktree-branch \"pr/{n}\"      // branch name\n  ```\n- **Conflicts**: an existing branch or directory of the same name aborts with an error notice, nothing is created. If a worktree already has that branch checked out, switch to it instead.\n- **Cleanup**: vig never removes worktrees (`git worktree remove` stays with the user). The Worktrees page lists them, so their state is visible.\n- **Read-only policy**: `git fetch` only adds to the object database and `git worktree add` leaves the current checkout untouched. Treat them as at least as safe as the already allowed `git switch`, allowed behind a confirmation dialog, and add them to the Allowed list in CLAUDE.md.\n- **KDL**: add `\"w\" \"OpenWorktree\"` to `pr_list` and `detail_view` under `page \"github\"`.\n- **Diff window integration** (after #200): when a worktree for the PR exists, `e` in the diff window opens the file from that path.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `w` shows the confirmation dialog; on approval fetch + worktree add run and the Worktrees page selects the new worktree\n- [ ] An existing worktree is reused instead of creating another\n- [ ] Works for PRs from forks\n- [ ] The three settings work from KDL and appear in the guide's Config Reference\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md's Allowed list gains `git fetch` / `git worktree add`\n- [ ] README / README.ja / the guide are updated (the demo needs a real fetch, so only show the worktree appearing in the existing Worktrees tape)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01N7wFSHbpTzvkK6WS1CRS7b","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-23T09:39:35Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":201,"state":"CLOSED","title":"GitHub page: open a PR as a worktree (`w`)"}
